{"name":"Matt Demon","hex":"#dd4433","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"matt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of matte."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of matte (“background, often painted or created with computers”).","Alternative spelling of mat (“an alloy in coppersmithing”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matt"},{"term":"demon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evil supernatural being.\nAn evil being resident in or working for Hell; a devil. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\n A false god or idol; a Satanic divinity. \n A very wicked or malevolent person; also  a mischievous person, especially a child. \nA source (especially personified) of great evil or wickedness; a destructive feeling or character flaw.","An evil being resident in or working for Hell; a devil. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Acronym of distinct electron motion particle: a quasiparticle, a type of massless neutral electron excitation associated with superconductivity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Matt Damon","blocks":[{"text":"Matthew Paige Damon is an American actor, film producer, and screenwriter. He was ranked among Forbes's most bankable stars in 2007, and in 2010 was one of the highest-grossing actors of all time. He has received various awards and nominations, including an Academy Award, an Actor Award, and two Golden Globe Awards, in addition to nominations for three British Academy Film Awards and seven Primetime Emmy Awards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/MattDamon-byPhilipRomano2.jpg/330px-MattDamon-byPhilipRomano2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matt_Damon","wikidata":"Q175535"},{"title":"Demon","blocks":[{"text":"A demon is an evil or malevolent supernatural entity, though they can be benevolent too. Historically, belief in demons, or stories about demons, occurs in folklore, mythology, religion, occultism, and literature; these beliefs are reflected in media including fiction, comics, film, television, and video games. Belief in demons probably goes back to the Paleolithic age, stemming from humanity's fear of the unknown, the strange and the horrific. In ancient Near Eastern religions and in the Abrahamic religions, including early Judaism and ancient-medieval Christian demonology, a demon is considered a harmful spiritual entity that may cause demonic possession, calling for an exorcism. Large portions of Jewish demonology, a key influence on Christianity and Islam, originated from a later form of Zoroastrianism, and was transferred to Judaism during the Persian era."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/PazuzuDemonAssyria1stMillenniumBCE_no_CGI_dropshadow_-_gradient_based_on.jpg/330px-PazuzuDemonAssyria1stMillenniumBCE_no_CGI_dropshadow_-_gradient_based_on.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demon","wikidata":"Q177413"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Matt_Damon_1999.jpg/250px-Matt_Damon_1999.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a6/Matt_Damon_1999.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Matt_Damon_1999.jpg/250px-Matt_Damon_1999.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Damon during filming for The Talented Mr. Ripley in 1999","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMatt_Damon_1999.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a9/Matt_Damon_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a9/Matt_Damon_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Damon in 2001","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMatt_Damon_2001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/MattDamonBU.jpg/500px-MattDamonBU.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/MattDamonBU.jpg/500px-MattDamonBU.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Damon attending an event for The Bourne Ultimatum in 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMattDamonBU.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Matt_Damon_2009_Venice_Film_Festival.jpg/330px-Matt_Damon_2009_Venice_Film_Festival.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Matt_Damon_2009_Venice_Film_Festival.jpg/330px-Matt_Damon_2009_Venice_Film_Festival.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Damon attending an event for The Informant! at the 2009 Venice International Film Festival","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMatt_Damon_2009_Venice_Film_Festival.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Matt_Damon_2014.jpg/500px-Matt_Damon_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Matt_Damon_2014.jpg/500px-Matt_Damon_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Damon at the French premiere of The Monuments Men in 2014","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMatt_Damon_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Matt_Damon_in